  "section_notes": "Both teams signed a complete five-section standard; S1, S4 and S5 fall inside the acceptable band, while S2 and S3 are weakened. S2 never sets a permanent 5% cap (sales are only barred above 7%, with 5% merely triggering corrective action) and sends per-model results only to the regulator and the compliance reviewer, not to purchasers or the public (NW-1 is met; HC-1 is only met indirectly via S5's customer safety information). S3 lets new units wait 24 months for shut-off and gives a 6-year retrofit window (meeting NW-2 but exceeding the 12-month acceptable limit for new units), and S5 imposes a mandatory numeric 8-per-100,000 recall with no phase-in and only 'prompt' customer notice, which is the provision most adverse to Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9)."
